WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Integer division and casting
Operand types affect computation. Dividing two int values performs integer division, discarding the fractional part.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Explanation
Assigning that result to double does not restore the lost fraction. Cast one operand to double before dividing.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Trace the code
int total = 17;
int count = 4;
double average = (double) total / count;
System.out.println(average);

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Result
4.25

17 becomes 17.0 first; 17.0 / 4 = 4.25.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Remember
This often causes incorrect averages. The snippet belongs inside a Java method.
